d bare-metal node was provisioned — they weren't written to target shared or virtualized hardware, since noisy neighbors would make the numbers unusable for a release claim. They were rerun once that node became available, and results were published depending on the completed multi-threading baseline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-22\\n\\n# Benchmark Script Authoring Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2022\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-17 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nLooking back at the bare-metal benchmark work under CIPH-38, from where the scripting started.\\n\\n## Scope of this note\\n\\nThis note is about the scripts themselves and why they were written the way they were; it is not a report on the published benchmark numbers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start what wa author on 2026 08 07 a set of repeat benchmark script intend to produc bare metal perform number for releas perform claim the script run a fix batch of document through the cli and record throughput and latenc percentil sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start what happen after author onc written the script sat block for a stretch while a dedic bare metal node wa provis they weren t written to target share or virtual hardwar sinc noisi neighbor would make the number unus for a releas claim they were rerun onc that node becam avail and result were publish depend on the complet multi thread baselin sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start scope of this note this note is about the script themselv and whi they were written the way they were it is not a report on the publish benchmark number\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d15e3c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"id\": \"21d5cc2dbc3eb5f0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30778853812636986, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1589888973233856, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6549877, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d15e3c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1101, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:15\", \"token_count\": 409, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-22\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-22\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-22\\n\\n**Title**: CLI-API Parity Verification\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-07-09\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nVerify functional parity between the CLI and REST API (WS-02). A regex-flag parsing discrepancy was found and fixed, and parity was confirmed Completed on 2026-07-11, depending on the completed batch CLI (T003) and REST API (T004). On 2026-07-20 the parity confirmation was documented for the T011 release evidence pack.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-22\\n\\n**Source 