calling it done; it depends on the batch CLI work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:21] Bob**: Nice turnaround. Good base for the large-file work to build on.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 31 slack thread batch worker pool integr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 08 56 charli wire the worker pool design into the batch cli now the design wa built to slot into the complet cli path so this is most plumb 2026 08 05 08 57 bob what s the default worker count go to be 2026 08 05 09 18 charli still tune it want to leav enough headroom that the pool doesn t starv the o and disk i o on a full batch run 2026 08 05 09 32 alic let u know onc you ve got someth we can run the core batch test against 2026 08 07 10 13 diana ran the core multi thread batch test against the integr pool pass clean against the exist batch cli baselin 2026 08 07 10 19 charli good that close out the integr call it done it depend on the batch cli work 2026 08 07 10 21 bob nice turnaround good base for the larg file work to build on\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e624e48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-batch-worker-pool-integration.md\", \"id\": \"240dfa63248b5344\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33626966726325747, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16666666751893924, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73201, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-batch-worker-pool-integration.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e624e48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-batch-worker-pool-integration.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-batch-worker-pool-integration.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1049, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:33\", \"token_count\": 320, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\nProfiling was opened after the T031 large-file chunking reopen surfaced memory growth on 2GB+ documents; the team wanted to confirm whether the loader itself, separate from the chunk-buffer issue being fixed under T031, was also retaining memory it shouldn't.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Tooling Constraint\\n\\nThe offline lab environment does not have the team's usual commercial profiler available (network-gated license check), so profiling switched to Python's stdlib `tracemalloc`, which works fully offline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Findings and Patch\\n\\nTracemalloc traced the retained allocations to the PDF loader's internal page-object cache, which was holding references to fully-parsed page objects long after the redaction pass for that page had completed. Bob patched the loader to explicitly drop the cache entry once a page's redaction pass finishes, rather than waiting for document close.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nRe-ran the same profiling pass post-patch: peak memory during a 2GB+ document run dropped to match the chunk-bounded footprint expected from the T031 chunking work, confirming the loader-side leak — distinct from the T031 buffer-release issue — is resolved.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Loader-side leak patched and verified; result depends on and complements the T031 chunking/buffer-release fix.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 trigger profil wa open after the t031 larg file chunk reopen surfac memori growth on 2gb document the team want to confirm whether the loader itself separ from the chunk buffer issu be fix under t031 wa also retain memori it shouldn t sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 tool constraint the offlin lab environ doe not have the team s usual commerci profil avail network gate licens check so profil switch to python s stdlib tracemalloc which work fulli offlin sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 find and patch tracemalloc trace the retain alloc to the pdf loader s intern page object cach which wa hold refer to fulli pars page object long after the redact pas for that page had complet bob patch the loader to explicit drop the cach entri onc a page s redact pas finish rather than wait for document close sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 valid re ran the same profil pas post patch peak memori dure a 2gb document run drop to match the chunk bound footprint expect from the t031 chunk work confirm the loader side leak distinct from the t031 buffer releas issu is resolv status complet loader side leak patch and verifi result depend on and complement the t031 chunk buffer releas fix\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9df68608a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"id\": \"f22e8883670ff4bd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3349107355608642, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1742424250869489, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70980346, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9df68608a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1441, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:00\", \"token_count\": 490, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProfile and patch memory-leak hotspots in the PDF loader following signals from the large-file chunking rework. Standard profiler tooling was unavailable in the offline lab, so the team switched to stdlib tracemalloc; the resulting leaks were patched, depending on the large-file chunking path.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Leak hotspots in the PDF loader are identified using an offline-compatible profiling tool.\\n\\n- Identified leaks are patched, verified against the large-file chunking dependency.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProfile and patch memory-leak hotspots in the PDF loader following signals from the large-file chunking rework. Standard profiler tooling was unavailable in the offline lab, so the team switched to stdlib tracemalloc; the resulting leaks were patched, depending on the large-file chunking path.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-15**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because memory-leak profiling is needed after the large-file chunking work.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-23**: Bob - Tracemalloc Patch (Completed)\\n\\n - *Patched PDF loader leaks found via tracemalloc, depending on the large-file chunking path.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 descript profil and patch memori leak hotspot in the pdf loader follow signal from the larg file chunk rework standard profil tool wa unavail in the offlin lab so the team switch to stdlib tracemalloc the result leak were patch depend on the larg file chunk path clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 accept criterion leak hotspot in the pdf loader are identifi use an offlin compat profil tool identifi leak are patch verifi against the larg file chunk depend clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 descript profil and patch memori leak hotspot in the pdf loader follow signal from the larg file chunk rework standard profil tool wa unavail in the offlin lab so the team switch to stdlib tracemalloc the result leak were patch depend on the larg file chunk path clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 activ histori 2026 08 15 alic task creat open open the task becaus memori leak profil is need after the larg file chunk work 2026 08 23 bob tracemalloc patch complet patch pdf loader leak found via tracemalloc depend on the larg file chunk path\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e982c6b48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"id\": \"6885e4b3a9768baf\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3219189219656507, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15909090995092962, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70185095, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e982c6b48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1050, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:18\", \"token_count\": 547,